# Data store (MongoDB)

This is a **document** store, not a relational database. Do not add SQL, Prisma, Drizzle, or SQLite. Access goes through `src/server/db/client.ts` + `src/server/db/collections.ts`.

## Documents

- Model what is read together as one document (embed extracted fields on a document; do not join them at read time).
- Reference (`id`) only when the related record is loaded independently (client, engagement).
- `$lookup` / application-level joins are a smell — denormalize or fetch in a repository helper that returns an already-shaped DTO.
- Collection name strings live only in `collectionNames`: `records`, `clients`, `engagements`, `documentTypes`, `requestTemplates`, `requestItems`, `documents` (`taxDocuments`), `activity`, `exports`. New collections get a typed helper in `collections.ts` in the same change.

## Schema lives in the app

Mongo will store whatever you insert. **Zod is the schema.**

- `safeParse` on HTTP input before write.
- `.parse` (or `safeParse` + 5xx) on documents after read — never return a raw driver doc to a route or the client.
- `fromStored` / `toStored` omit top-level `null` and `undefined`. The Mongo driver serializes `undefined` as `null`, which fails Zod `.optional()` fields; nested nulls (extraction `value: null`) stay.
- Infer TS types from those schemas (`src/shared/schemas/`). Do not keep a second Mongo-only type that diverges.

## Tenant / client scope

When records are client-scoped, every query includes `clientId` (or equivalent). Missing filter is a bug. Cross-client reads return 404, not 403.

## Indexes and env

- A new query predicate gets an index defined in the same change (helper or documented setup).
- URI and db name come from `config` (`MONGODB_URI`, `MONGODB_DB`). Empty URI → in-memory server (dev/test). Do not hardcode hosts.
- An empty database auto-seeds the demo book (`seedIfEmpty` on API boot; `bun run seed` / `bun run seed -- --reset` from the CLI). Seed reads `demo-docs/figures.json` so extracted figures match the tracked PDFs.

## Anti-patterns

`find({})` on a client-scoped collection. Returning `_id` ObjectIds through the API (this app uses string ids). Trusting stored JSON without Zod. SQL-shaped table-per-field models. Mocking `MongoClient` in tests that claim to prove persistence.
